# Derived local palette content depends on licensed user library packages. Rebuild with
# create_local_architecture.py / create_local_prop_materials.py; do not redistribute.
unreal/TornVeilOnline/Content/TornVeil/LocalPalette/
unreal/TornVeilOnline/Content/TornVeil/Materials/LocalPalette/
# The Ashford garment meshes are project-owned geometry, but each one embeds the City Sample
# clothing skeleton's reference pose and binds to `SK_Base`, so on a machine without that
# licensed pack they are 19 MB of assets that cannot load. Same call as LocalPalette above: the
# generator is the source of truth. Rebuild with
#   blender --background --python art/tools/ashford_garments/build_garments.py
#   unreal/scripts/Run-EditorPython.ps1 -Script unreal/scripts/import_ashford_garments.py -Render
# `M_TV_AshfordCloth` is deliberately NOT ignored: it contains no vendor data, it is 12 KB, and
# the shader that decides what this culture looks like should be reviewable. Re-running the
# importer rebuilds it, so expect it to show as modified after an import.
unreal/TornVeilOnline/Content/TornVeil/Characters/Ashford/
unreal/scripts/__pycache__/
.unrealmcp.json

